 other  two completely separate instances not  related  thank you and good afternoon my name is  deputy chief jim siebach  i'm one of the two patrol deputy chiefs  over our patrol division  i've worked these protests since they  started this past  several days  let me first convey  thanks to those in the community our  first responder partners and all those  that have reached out to us  to show support for us and the families  of our  injured officer  your thoughts and prayers are much  appreciated  i also want to say that what we're  seeing is not indicative of the  community i've policed over the last 27  years nor does it look like the  community that we all know and love and  what we're seeing is not representative  of what we all know las vegas to be  i also want to reiterate as sheriff  lombardo has said from the beginning  that these events that sparked these  protests are inconsistent  with the training and protocols of the  lvmpd  we are also sickened by what we saw that  sparked all of this as an agency and  from the patrol division  we respect everyone's constitutional  right to protest we are here to support  you  and to keep you safe as long as it's  done lawfully  unfortunately that isn't what we've been  seeing  what we as an agency are consistently  seeing over these last few days  is that these protests  these protests start out peacefully  with all the good intentions for  significant change to spark the  conversation  and  hear what people ex allow people to  express what they want to say  but as the night goes on the good  intended and law-abiding people leave  and those that seek to break the law  stay behind these people are clearly  not here for peaceful purposes  they are set on damaging our community  our businesses and to cause harm to our  officers and the people in the area  i watched firsthand from the streets  from our command post how these  criminals are trying to leverage these  peaceful demonstrations to their  advantage  over the f