ntly trained all of our  department on the new policy that  included way before these incidents that  happen that includes putting people in a  recovery position as soon as possible  after an arrest  the goal of lvmpd is to continue to grow  and partner with our community  finally i just ask for the public to  please continue to pray for our officer  and all that is going on in our  community  thank you  is there any indication these groups are  well organized or i've heard reports of  other cities possibly having out of  state instigators or have you identified  any of that i don't have enough  information to answer that the  information that i have seen is the  majority are still local  yes  we've been down on the street there are  obviously thousands of officers down  there  around the subway someone breaks into  your house you call 9-1-1 who comes  right now  we still have officers policing our  community keeping us safe we've been  bringing in officers extra on overtime  we've had great partnerships with  henderson and north las vegas city  marshals night county nhp uh parole and  probation all of our partners are coming  together to keep southern nevada safe  i know we're coming up on the sixth year  since officer  soldo and officer beck were slain how  heavy does this weigh on the department  this impacts all of our officers but it  also reminds our it reminds everyone of  the dangers of our job  it reminds everyone that the commitment  that these officers these men and women  take every day to serve our community  and it does strengthen their resolve to  want to do the best that they can and we  have tremendous leadership here at this  department that continues to provide the  support  the  wellness services to our officers and to  their families and we are checking the  pulse of the morale every single day to  make sure our officers are ready and  prepared before they hit the streets  sir how do you differentiate between  those people who are there for good  intentions and those people who are not  we allowed these protests to occur we  allow them to stay lawfully on the  sidewalks sometimes when it gets too big  they have to go onto the streets  last night for example  we made room for them we tried to block  traffic  we even moved officers back away so the  protesters could go through but a  contingent remained behind as i said  last night the crowd was probably around  three thousand uh and the majority of  them started marching peacefully back  but a good number and say approximately  three to five hundred stayed behind and  then they begin to  do actions such as you saw there  yes  how do you find that balance between  there's been a lot of talk about  bringing in people with riot gear stuff  like that how it could potentially  escalate situations more national guard  how do you find a balance between  escalating the situation and then also  showing a sign of authority like we're  seeing up in minneapolis for example  what i'll speak to here locally is we  did provide our officers with  protective equipment because of the  items that were being thrown if you  notice on the first day a lot of our  officers were not wearing that gear and  we did have a lot of officers injured  and so again  we give the people the opportunity to  do their  constitution constitutionally protected  activity lawfully and when they're not  we provide them an opportunity to stop  we give them a dispersal order and we  ask them to move on and if not then we  have to take the appropriate action  yes in the back  now we know these people have paragons  they'll probably change their strategy  with when you go to these places  and  have some with these people i'm sorry i  didn't hear the first part of your  question  well now we know these people have  partners right so you will change your  strategy when you go to these places  and confront these people  uh our officer safety uh is always at  the utmost uh every day we try to learn  lessons 